    "result_text": "Typecheck passes cleanly. The change is complete and verified.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented a full-stack change letting you **change or remove charge (line-item) lines on an invoice, with the total recomputing** \u2014 the acceptance test passes.\n\n**Server (OfficeFloor + Spring):**\n- `InvoiceLineItemRemove.java` \u2014 `POST /api/invoices/{id}/lineitems/{lineItemId}/remove`: deletes the line (404 if the invoice/line is unknown or the line doesn't belong to the invoice) and recomputes the invoice's stored `amount = sum(qty \u00d7 unitPrice)`.\n- `InvoiceLineItemUpdate.java` \u2014 `POST /api/invoices/{id}/lineitems/{lineItemId}`: validates and saves new `{description, qty, unitPrice}`, same recompute (400 on invalid input, 404 on unknown).\n- Two new endpoint YAMLs wiring those classes under `rest/api/invoices/{id}/lineitems/...` (additive, one file per endpoint). Reused the existing `NewLineItem` body and `LineItemRepository`/`InvoiceRepository`.\n\n**Front-end (additive, new files + rule-3 region edit):**\n- `slots/defs/lineItemRow.ts` \u2014 declares a new `lineitem.row` slot region for per-line actions.\n- `features/lineitems/actions.slot.tsx` \u2014 fills that region with **Change** (inline edit) and **Remove** controls; each write is a `useMutation` that invalidates `['lineitems', invoiceId]`, so the list and its client-derived total re-query and stay in step for free. Carries `data-testid=\"lineitem-remove-{id}\"` (what the test clicks) plus edit/save/cancel testids.\n- `features/lineitems/queries.ts` \u2014 added `removeLineItem` / `updateLineItem` (via the existing `postJson`, since `api/http.ts` is pinned and has no DELETE helper \u2014 consistent with the existing send/pay POST actions).\n- `LineItemsTable.tsx` \u2014 the one sanctioned edit: rendering the new `<LineItemRow.Slot>` in each row (rule 3, \"render the region with `<X.Slot>`\").\n\n**No migration or seed change was needed** \u2014 the `invoice_line_items` table and the `/__test__` seed already support line items.\n\nThe test verifies removing \"Hosting\" ($50) from a $150 invoice drops the row count to 1 and the `invoice-amount` to `$100.00` \u2014 passing. No schema/seed change was required because the line-item table and seed path already existed.",
